; Kepler's problem, a body about a fixed centre of unit mass (G = 1),
; stepped by Stormer-Verlet: the first reference that divides and takes a
; root at run time. r3 = |q|^3 is one root and a product; each force
; component one division by it, so a step runs three routines, inlined
; (docs/LANGUAGE.md, "The operations"; parcel C4). An image with them
; needs revision 8's flag control: the software targets run it.
system kepler
format fp64
round  rne
state  x, y, px, py
let r2 = fma(x, x, y * y)
let r3 = r2 * sqrt(r2)
d/dt x  = px
d/dt y  = py
d/dt px = -(x / r3)
d/dt py = -(y / r3)
step   stormer-verlet, h = 1/100, q = (x, y), p = (px, py)
